    "quality": { "value": 9, "reasoning": "Extremely clear and actionable. The table format for the parallel work strategy is immediately useful. The contracts-as-code examples give teams something tangible. The 30-minute meeting agenda is practical and time-boxed. The language is direct without being dismissive of the teams' frustrations." },
    "persona": { "value": 8, "reasoning": "Strong Juanita Marquez voice - the linguistic framing ('implementation must work at the linguistic level', 'Code and language are the same thing. Both program minds.') is very much her character. The focused intensity and pattern-recognition feel authentic. The confidence in making decisions and the 'I understand how it works' closing are well-placed. Could have incorporated more of her specific background in religious iconography or information visualization." }
  },
